The boot pool's own node stays a root rather than hanging below the root task's memory,
so an Untyped covers a pool that does not lie below it,
and revoking below that Untyped would not reach the root task's objects.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: memory that may hold kernel objects overlaps a node not above or below it

diff --git a/kernel/boot.c b/kernel/boot.c
--- a/kernel/boot.c
+++ b/kernel/boot.c
@@ -62,7 +62,6 @@ struct thread *boot_create_root(void)
         kpanic("cannot fill the root task's table");
     }
     struct cap *root_ram = &table->slots[BOOT_CAP_ROOT_RAM];
-    cap_attach(root_ram, &pool->node);
 
     /*
      * Below the pool's node, as every capability to an object of the pool is,
